{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"HARD ANODIZING"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore (D12) has a tight tolerance band of 0.018 mm, but the part is hard anodized and no allowance or note accounts for the coating thickness on this fit surface. The anodize layer will shrink the bore and may prevent assembly with the mating shaft; the designer should either increase the bore size to allow for the coating or add a note specifying masking or re-machining after anodizing."

    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Increase the bore size to allow for the coating or add a note specifying masking or re-machining after anodizing."}]}
